new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bf372ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/path/chopgimp-vobject.h
@@ -0,0 +1,431 @@
+/* GIMP - The GNU Image Manipulation Program
+ * chopgimp-vobject.h — ChopGimp 3.27: vector layers with several objects
+ *
+ * A GimpVectorLayer holds an ordered tree of objects (paths and groups),
+ * each with its own name, geometry, transformation, fill, stroke,
+ * opacity, blend mode, visibility, lock and live path effects. GIMP's
+ * vector layer is improved rather than doubled: its own path and its
+ * fill / stroke options stay the « legacy view » of the objects:
+ *
+ *  - the legacy path (layer->options->path, in the Paths panel and in
+ *    the XCF) holds the sub-paths of ALL the objects, bottom to top, in
+ *    image coordinates (transformations applied, before live effects);
+ *  - the legacy fill / stroke are those of object #1 (the first leaf,
+ *    bottom-most);
+ *  - every edit of the legacy path (path tool, scripts, layer and image
+ *    transformations, undo of those) is spread back to the objects by
+ *    sub-path; a new sub-path joins the object of the sub-path before it;
+ *    an object whose sub-paths are all deleted stays, empty, until the
+ *    next save; every edit of the legacy fill / stroke goes to object #1.
+ *
+ *  A layer that was never edited as objects keeps GIMP's renderer
+ *  (pixel-identical to 3.26): it is « legacy » until the first object
+ *  edit. The objects are saved in the XCF parasite « chopgimp-vobjects »
+ *  (SVG-like XML, see chopgimp-vobject.c).
+ *
+ *  CHOPGIMP_NO_VOBJECTS=1 turns all of this off (3.26 behaviour).
+ *
+ * Coordinates: image pixels. obj->path is in the object's local space,
+ * obj->transform maps local → parent space (the parent group's local
+ * space; the root group has the identity). Gradient coordinates are
+ * relative to the object's bounding box (SVG objectBoundingBox: 0..1).
+ *
+ * Changing objects: always use the functions below (they push the undo
+ * step, re-render the dirty area, update the legacy path and emit
+ * « objects-changed »). A tool which edits obj->path in place during a
+ * drag calls chopgimp_vlayer_push_undo() once at the start, then
+ * chopgimp_vlayer_object_changed() after every change.
+ *
+ * Signals of GimpVectorLayer (registered in gimpvectorlayer.c):
+ *   "objects-changed"          (GimpVectorLayer *, gpointer dirty)
+ *       dirty: const GeglRectangle * in image coordinates, or NULL
+ *       when the whole layer changed (structure, undo, load…)
+ *   "object-selection-changed" (GimpVectorLayer *)
+ *
